tasks.description:
Fixes review findings P108-R9, P108-R11, P108-R12 and P108-R15. The journal writer and the commit-time detector must recognise the same identity shapes.

- Detector shapes in the writer. tools/check-committed-pii.py flags session-slug, tempdir-session, escaped-path and unexpanded-home. Move these into _journal_io as shared pattern objects, the way MACHINE_PATH_SHAPES already is, so the detector reads the same objects. machine_path_shape reads them too, so redacted_free_text replaces them and check_free_text refuses them. The one deliberate difference stays: a relative path whose first segment is home.
- File URLs. A token may start after a URL scheme's slashes, so a file URL into a home directory is refused at the door, redacted in a plugin row, and flagged by the detector. An https URL whose path merely contains the word Users stays allowed.
- More flags at the door. Values of --gate, --gate-set, scope's --gate and done's --verified-by go through the same check_free_text door before the lock, like the prose flags.
- Symlinks. Redaction decides inside or outside on the realpath, but relativises the normalised spelling when that spelling lies under the root. A path through a symlinked directory therefore keeps the spelling the writer used.

Cases, each in both directions:
- each detector shape, redacted in a hook row and refused at the audit-task door;
- a file URL refused, redacted and flagged, with an https allow twin;
- a retarget --gate carrying a home path refused, with a plain-command twin allowed;
- a symlinked directory keeps its own spelling.

Fixes review findings P108-R10, P108-R13, P108-R14 and P108-R16. A shell write gets its bare form's verdict in every spelling the shell arm reads, and a quoted argument is not read as a redirect.

- cp, mv and install. A last operand that resolves at the effective cwd to an existing directory is read as a directory, so the source's name inside it is the target. This holds even when the directory is spelled without a trailing slash.
- Nesting depth. When the handed-command walk reaches its depth bound and a further handed command exists, that command is graded unresolved at the deny tier rather than read as nothing.
- Interpreter writes. The interpreter write grammar reads a keyword mode= (for example mode='a' or mode='w') as well as the positional mode, for the journal arm and the source arm alike.
- Redirect and tee. Handed commands are already graded through their own views, so the redirect and tee arms skip matches inside quotes, as the in-place arm does. A commit message that mentions a redirect, and a handed cd that leaves the tree, are no longer read as writes. A handed redirect is read once, at its own cwd.

Cases, each with an allow twin:
- cp onto an existing directory with no slash;
- a nesting one level past the bound;
- open with a keyword mode, against the journal and a source file, at each tier;
- a commit message containing a redirect;
- a handed cd out of the tree followed by a redirect.

test_hooks.py's contract rows cover the new shapes. KNOWN_DIVERGENCE lists any shape still left open, with its reason.

SECURITY.md describes the journal door, the redaction and the shell arm as P108.13 and P108.14 leave them:
- which caller flags are asked at the door;
- which identity shapes the writer and the detector share;
- the shell arm's directory, nesting, keyword-mode and quoted-redirect behaviour;
- the residual list, stating every shape still open and nothing already closed.

Every sentence must be true of the committed code of the two tasks this one depends on.

Fixes review findings P108-R21 and P108-R22. The shared identity shapes match what names a machine, and nothing else.

session-slug is narrowed to a real slug's shape: more than the user segment after -Users- or -home-, or a path separator around it. A whitespace-led word such as -home-dir, or -Users-bob alone in prose, no longer matches. Every real slug placement the detector reads is still caught. unexpanded-home stays refused at the door, because the commit-time detector fails the build on it. The code says so beside the shape, so the choice is recorded rather than accidental.

For the file scheme only, a token may start after file://<host>, so a file URL naming a host before a home directory is refused, redacted and flagged. An https URL with the same path stays allowed.

Cases:
- prose with -home-dir and -Users-bob is allowed;
- every real slug placement is denied;
- file://localhost is refused, redacted and flagged, with an https twin;
- check-committed-pii's selftest carries the same allow and deny pairs.

check-committed-pii must still exit 0 on the tree.

Fixes review finding P108-R28. Every real home slug placement is caught again, and prose is still left alone.

session-slug accepts the lone user segment wherever a non-whitespace delimiter, or a text or line boundary, bounds it: a quote, =, :, (, or the start or end of a line. This covers a JSON value, a key=value, and the Windows home slug C--Users-<name>. Only whitespace-led prose, such as an option named -home-dir or a lone dash-led user word in a sentence, is left alone.

sp10 and q2f gain rows for:
- a quoted JSON value;
- a key=value;
- a line start;
- the Windows spelling.
Each comes with a prose allow twin.

check-committed-pii must still exit 0 on the tree.

Fixes review findings P108-R31 to P108-R34. A trailing slash never changes a copy's verdict, and a wide copy stays within the hook's time budget.

- A whole copy or move (mv, or cp -r/-R/-a) onto a slash-ended destination that does not exist, and that no earlier clause made, lands as the destination itself, so it is read the way the slashless operand is read. Record as a residual the platform split for a slash-ended source onto an existing directory (BSD copies the contents, GNU copies the directory).
- Directories under a toplevel git has already answered are resolved by containment, with no further git call. If that is not enough, bound the expansion by directory count, and report what is past the bound as not established.
- SECURITY.md:
  - an out-of-project destination root is one destination;
  - the symlinked-subdirectory edge;
  - no count before the residual list;
  - the lone-slug residual shapes are named: option or value text read as a slug, and a whitespace-led slug in a value position.
- t11's fixture root carries no slug shape.

Cases:
- cp -r src/ lib/ and mv src/ lib/ allowed against a plan declaring lib/app.ts, each with a block twin where lib exists;
- a wide copy into a linked worktree whose git call count is bounded by toplevels;
- t11 run under a slug-shaped temp root.
